From da2d9fbe58dbdea90a0db680cb329ff034368ba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ada Lundhe <adalundhe@lundhe.audio>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:42:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] D189, PM M421: a window's change is counted before its
 lock is let go. A vCPU's fault that waited for the lock read the old count,
 and a second fault at one address at that count was taken for the guest's
 own: a live range's load read a bus's 0xff and its store was lost

Window::reconcile and evict counted after dropping the table; map, map_zeros and unmap already counted under it. On jupiter, 3 runs: 0 fell through at 2, 4 and 8 vCPUs in 6,400 followings each, 7,347 to 13,640 faults run again. Reaches a share's own file alone, as a server's section is never followed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/fs/window_whp.rs | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/fs/window_whp.rs b/crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/fs/window_whp.rs
index 489d52fb..8fe9973f 100644
--- a/crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/fs/window_whp.rs
+++ b/crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/fs/window_whp.rs
@@ -865,9 +865,13 @@ impl Window {
                 changed = true;
             }
         }
-        drop(table);
+        // Counted before the lock goes: a vCPU whose fault waited for it must read a count past
+        // this change, or it takes a live range's fault for the guest's own (PM M421).
         if changed {
             self.changes.fetch_add(1, Ordering::AcqRel);
+        }
+        drop(table);
+        if changed {
             self.restored.notify_all();
         }
     }
@@ -898,10 +902,11 @@ impl Window {
             e.evicted = true;
             changed = true;
         }
-        drop(table);
+        // Counted before the lock goes, as [`Window::reconcile`] does.
         if changed {
             self.changes.fetch_add(1, Ordering::AcqRel);
         }
+        drop(table);
     }
 
     /// A guest's access to memory the host could not give, at `gpa`, which WHP's memory
